  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast bias when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) — model tends to overestimate prices.",
    "Adjust downward for long-term (30d) forecasts when recent prices show strong downward momentum (e.g., 3 consecutive days < 70).",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if forecast is > 10% above recent 5-day average — especially after spikes.",
    "Lower forecast if sentiment history shows increasing negative sentiment (e.g., 3+ consecutive negative values).",
    "Increase forecast slightly if sentiment is positive and price is trending downward — model underreacts to bullish sentiment.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in forecasts when history shows high volatility — use 15-day moving average as a floor."
  ]
}
